.nh
.TH "PB-CONFIG-STATUS-BAR-SET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-status-bar-set - Set a status-bar preference


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config status-bar set <key> <value> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set a status-bar preference

.PP
Set one status-bar preference by key and value. Preview the result before using it in a full-screen terminal application.

.PP
The status bar is rendered by the interactive terminal client. Preferences affect local presentation and do not change remote sessions. Use preview to inspect the result before relying on a theme or width setting.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-status-bar(1)\fP
